  <h1>Emergency Boiler Callout Prices in York: What You'll Actually Pay</h1>
  <p>When your boiler's gone and the house is getting cold, the last thing you want is to ring round for a price and get "it depends" from three different companies. So here's the actual number, no games: our <a href="/boiler-repairs-breakdowns/">emergency boiler repair</a> call-out in York is £120, and that's what you pay — no VAT to add on top.</p>

  <h2>What the £120 actually covers</h2>
  <p>That fee covers the visit and a proper diagnosis — an engineer coming to your house, having a genuine look at what's wrong with your boiler, and telling you straight what's caused it. It's not a "foot in the door" fee that then balloons once someone's stood in your kitchen. If your boiler breakdown turns out to be something quick — a reset, a fault with the pressure, a stuck valve — that £120 is very often the whole bill.</p>

  <h2>What's actually included in the visit</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>An engineer travelling out to you, not a call centre reading from a script</li>
    <li>A proper diagnosis of what's wrong — not a guess based on what you've described over the phone</li>
    <li>A straight explanation of the fault in plain English, so you understand what's happened and why</li>
    <li>A written price for any further work, before anything else is touched</li>
  </ul>
  <p>That's the whole point of a fixed call-out fee — you know exactly what you're paying just to get someone qualified out to look at the problem, separate from whatever the fix itself ends up costing.</p>

  <h2>Why we don't do the old "cheap callout, huge invoice" trick</h2>
  <p>A lot of people ringing about a boiler not working in York have been caught out before — quoted a low number to get someone through the door, then hit with a much bigger bill once the engineer's already in the house and they feel stuck. We do it the other way round: one clear call-out price, and if it turns out you need parts or further work, that gets priced and agreed with you before we lift a finger, not after. You get a written quote, you say yes or no, and only then do we carry on.</p>

  <h2>When it costs more than £120</h2>
  <p>Straightforwardly: when the job needs more than diagnosis and a quick fix. If a part's failed and needs replacing, or the repair takes longer than a standard visit, that additional cost is quoted upfront and agreed with you before it's added to the bill. And occasionally, a breakdown reveals that the boiler itself is on its last legs rather than worth patching up again — in which case we'll tell you honestly, rather than keep charging you to repair something that's not really fixable long-term.</p>

  <h2>Same-day boiler repair, same honest price</h2>
  <p>Whether it's a same day boiler repair because you've genuinely got no heating in York on a freezing morning, or something that can wait for a normal appointment, the £120 call-out figure doesn't change depending on how urgent it feels. We'd rather you knew the real number before you pick up the phone than find out afterwards.</p>

  <h2>If someone vulnerable is affected, say so</h2>
  <p>A good chunk of the calls we get are from people worried about an elderly parent, a young family, or someone unwell being left without heating — not just about the money. If that's your situation, tell us straight away when you ring. It doesn't change the £120 call-out figure, but it does change how we prioritise getting to you, because a cold house is a much bigger deal for some households than others.</p>

  <h2>Get a straight answer, no obligation</h2>
  <p>If your boiler's broken down and you want to know roughly what you're looking at before booking anyone, just call us and tell us what's happening. We'll give you an honest steer on urgency and cost over the phone — not a script designed to get you to say yes. Call us on <a href={siteConfig.phoneHref}>{siteConfig.phoneDisplay}</a> or WhatsApp <a href={`https://wa.me/${siteConfig.whatsappNumberIntl}`}>{siteConfig.whatsappDisplay}</a>, and we'll take it from there.</p>
